{%- comment -%}
  ORI pre-order state
  ===================
  Outputs 'pre' when a variant should be sold as a pre-order rather than an
  ordinary add to cart, and nothing at all otherwise. Capture it:

    {%- capture ori_preorder -%}
      {%- render 'ori-preorder-state', product: product, variant: some_variant -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign ori_preorder = ori_preorder | strip -%}

  Why this exists rather than reading variant.available:

  With "Sell when out of stock" switched on (inventory_policy 'continue')
  Shopify keeps reporting a variant as available no matter how far past zero it
  goes. Every buy button in this theme gated on .available, so a product sitting
  at -1 rendered a live, enabled Add to cart. Checking the tracked quantity is
  the only thing that actually answers "has this run out".

  quantity_rule_soldout is not reusable for this: it switches itself off under
  'continue', which is the exact case we care about.

  All three conditions matter:

  - inventory_management == 'shopify'. Untracked variants have a meaningless
    quantity, so they are never pre-order and keep their normal Add to cart.
  - inventory_quantity <= 0. There is nothing on the shelf.
  - inventory_policy == 'continue'. This is the one that separates a pre-order
    from a plain sell out. "Sell when out of stock" being switched on is the
    merchant saying orders past zero are still wanted, which is what a pre-order
    is. With 'deny' at zero stock Shopify refuses the add anyway, so the product
    is simply sold out and must keep saying so. Timesact draws the same line: its
    isVariantOutOfStock() returns true for DENY at zero and shows out of stock
    rather than a pre-order.

  Deliberately NOT covered here:

  - Tag driven pre-order and special order. Those are the existing ORI flow and
    open an enquiry modal instead of taking money, so they stay on their own
    so_type path. This is only about stock running out.

  Anything unexpected has to land on "sell it as normal", never on "hide the
  button".
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign v = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign state = ''

  if v and v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_quantity <= 0 and v.inventory_policy == 'continue'
    assign state = 'pre'
  endif

  echo state
-%}
